      "title": "Classic Approach: Coarse-Grained MD",
      "classification": "substantive",
      "coverage": "covered",
      "text": [
        "Classic Approach: Coarse-Grained MD",
        "Coarse-grained MD (1) groups a set of atoms into beads, (2) define force",
        "field on beads, (3) simulate beads.",
        "• Pros: (1) Remove fast degree of freedom → smooth landscape → longer MD step (~1ps)",
        "(2) Reduced input size → Faster force field calculation",
        "• Cons: (1) Inaccurate and unable to model some phenomena (e.g. hydrogen bond, ligand binding)",
        "(2) Lose transferability, biased dynamic observables.",
        "10"
      ],
      "media_sha256": [
        "2b4069de0ec2d9fb8d37793b1179a33debb91d909ab3c8adec8bbde0b239d1ff",
